<main>
  <p class="eyebrow">henk</p>
  <h1>Nothing is linked to this hostname.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    henk answered, so the stack is up — it just has no project registered under this name.
    Every <code>*.{{TLD}}</code> name resolves to henk whether or not it's linked, so the
    hostname working proves nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>Most likely causes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>A typo in the hostname.</strong>
      <p>
        <code>henk status</code> lists every linked project and the <code>.{{TLD}}</code>
        host it answers on.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The project was never linked.</strong>
      <p>
        Run <code>henk link</code> in the project directory. For an extra hostname on an
        already-linked project, <code>henk link --add --host &lt;sub&gt; --port &lt;port&gt;</code>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="fix">
    <strong><code>henk status</code></strong> shows what's linked and where it points.
  </p>
</main>
